# Spec 021 — Production token guard (no silent fixture mode)

Status: Draft
Owner: <you>
Related: 004-backend-hardening (health probe), 006-deployment (Render
secrets, CI smoke test)

## Overview

A missing `MAPBOX_TOKEN` in production must be loud, not invisible. Today
the backend treats a blank token as "fixture mode" everywhere, so a freshly
created Render service (dashboard secrets are per service and do not carry
over) serves the committed Seattle polygon for every pin, every time, every
mode — the map shows one static "Midday" ring that ignores the pin, and
`/api/health` says everything is fine. This spec confines fixture mode to
local dev and explicit opt-in, and makes the token's absence observable.

## Context

- Incident (2026-09-14): the service was recreated as `livenear` to get a
  clean URL. The new service had no `MAPBOX_TOKEN`; `/api/isochrone`
  returned the fixture (200) for Seattle and Spokane alike while geocode and
  commute returned 503 "no token configured". Diagnosis took a live-API
  byte comparison against the fixture file.
- `serve_fixture` in `config.py` is the single switch; `STATIC_DIR` is only
  ever set in the production image (006 R2), so it is a reliable "this is a
  deploy, not a laptop" signal without adding a new env var.
- The frontend already renders a 503 from `/api/isochrone` honestly
  ("Commute layer unavailable" toast, 005), so failing is strictly better
  UX than a fake contour.

## Requirements

- **R1 — No fixture in production.** `serve_fixture` is true only when
  `USE_FIXTURE=true`, or when the token is blank AND `STATIC_DIR` is unset.
  With `STATIC_DIR` set and no token, `/api/isochrone` returns 503
  `isochrone unavailable (no token configured)` — matching the geocode and
  commute endpoints — and makes no upstream call.
- **R2 — Health reports the mode.** `/api/health` gains
  `"isochrone": "live" | "fixture" | "unavailable"` so one curl tells an
  operator whether the deploy has its token.
- **R3 — Startup warning.** When the token is blank the app logs a WARNING
  at startup naming the consequence (fixture served in dev / commute
  endpoints disabled in production).
- **R4 — CI and docs follow.** The Docker smoke test opts in with
  `USE_FIXTURE=true` and asserts `"isochrone":"fixture"`; a second run with
  no env asserts the guard (`"unavailable"`, isochrone 503). README,
  `render.yaml`, and `.env.example` describe the new URL, the per-service
  secret, and the health check to run after any redeploy.

## Non-functional / Constraints

- Local dev without a token is unchanged: fixture isochrone, no Mapbox calls.
- No new environment variables; no frontend change required.
- The token still never leaves the backend (001 R5).

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] R1: `pytest` — production settings (`static_dir` set, blank token)
      yield 503 from `/api/isochrone` with no upstream request; the same
      settings plus `use_fixture=True` yield the single fixture band.
- [ ] R2: `/api/health` returns `"isochrone": "live"` with a token,
      `"fixture"` in dev without one, `"unavailable"` in production without
      one (unit tests + CI smoke).
- [ ] R3: starting the backend with a blank token prints the WARNING.
- [ ] R4: CI docker job passes both smoke runs; README/render.yaml name
      livenear.onrender.com and the health check.
